# Testing Standards

## Test Tiers

| Tier | Path | DB | Marker | Speed |
|------|------|-----|--------|-------|
| Unit | `tests/unit/` | No | — | Fast |
| Property | `tests/properties/` | No | `@pytest.mark.property` | Fast |
| Smoke | `tests/test_startup_smoke.py` | No | — | Fast |
| Contract | `tests/contract/` | PostgreSQL + Redis | `@pytest.mark.contract` | Slow |

## Unit Test Rules

- No DB, no HTTP calls, no file I/O
- Mock external dependencies with `unittest.mock.MagicMock`
- One assertion per test when possible
- Name: `test_{what}_{condition}_{expected}`

```python
# tests/unit/test_loans_service.py
def test_borrow_book_decrements_available_copies():
    from app.api.v1.loans.services import borrow_book
    from unittest.mock import MagicMock
    book = MagicMock(available_copies=2)
    db = MagicMock()
    db.scalar.return_value = book          # locked book row
    db.get.return_value = MagicMock()      # member exists
    borrow_book(db, book_id=1, member_id=1)
    assert book.available_copies == 1
    db.commit.assert_called_once()
```

## Contract Test Rules

- Always start with `docker compose up postgres redis -d`
- Mark with `@pytest.mark.contract` at module level
- Mark write operations with `@pytest.mark.mutation`
- Use `seeded_user` fixture for authenticated requests

```python
# tests/contract/test_books.py
import pytest
pytestmark = pytest.mark.contract

def test_list_books_returns_200(contract_client, seeded_user):
    resp = contract_client.get("/api/v1/books/", headers=seeded_user["headers"])
    assert resp.status_code == 200
    assert "items" in resp.json()
    assert "total" in resp.json()

@pytest.mark.mutation
def test_create_book_persists(contract_client, seeded_user):
    resp = contract_client.post(
        "/api/v1/books/",
        json={"title": "Dune", "author": "Herbert", "isbn": "978-0441013593", "total_copies": 3},
        headers=seeded_user["headers"],
    )
    assert resp.status_code == 201
    book_id = resp.json()["id"]
    fetch = contract_client.get(f"/api/v1/books/{book_id}", headers=seeded_user["headers"])
    assert fetch.status_code == 200
```

## Property Test Rules

```python
# tests/properties/test_pagination.py
from hypothesis import given, settings, strategies as st
import pytest

pytestmark = pytest.mark.property

@given(
    page=st.integers(min_value=1, max_value=500),
    page_size=st.integers(min_value=1, max_value=100),
)
@settings(max_examples=200)
def test_skip_is_always_non_negative(page: int, page_size: int):
    skip = (page - 1) * page_size
    assert skip >= 0
```

## What Tests Must Cover for New Endpoints

| Scenario | Tier |
|----------|------|
| Happy path (200/201) | Contract |
| Not found (404) | Contract |
| Conflict — no copies / double return (409) | Contract |
| Unauthenticated (401) | Contract |
| Forbidden (403) | Contract |
| Service logic (borrow/return atomicity, validation) | Unit |
| Input shape invariants | Property |

## Running Tests

```bash
uv run pytest tests/unit/ tests/properties/ -q              # Fast tier
uv run pytest tests/contract/ -m "contract and not mutation" -q  # Read-only contract
uv run pytest tests/contract/ -m mutation -q                # Mutation contract
uv run pytest --cov=app --cov-report=html                   # Full with coverage
```
